DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260926T180000
DTSTAMP:20260718T212955Z
URL:https://jackofthewood.com/events/nobodys-darling-string-band-3-2026-09
 -05-2026-09-12-2026-09-19-2026-09-26/
SUMMARY:NOBODY'S DARLING STRING BAND
DESCRIPTION:\nNobody’s Darling String Band plays lively music in the old-
 time tradition at Jack of the Wood Pub every Saturday afternoon from 4-6pm
 .\n\n\n\nBand Members include Dona Cavanagh\, fiddle\; Zena Rubin\, banjo-
 uke\; Maxine Herring\, rhythm guitar\; Hilary Dirlam\, melody guitar\; and
  Celia Millington-Wyckoff\, bass.\n\n\n\nThe five women comprising Nobody
 ’s Darling each have a long history of playing old-time music. Individua
 lly they have played in many other bands through the years\, including The
  Carolina Oldtimers\, The Pegtwisters\, The Zuma House Band\, Too Hot To C
 ook\, The Luke Smathers Mountain Swing Band\, Honey Holler\, and The Carol
 ina Chick Peas.\n\n\n\nStop in to enjoy the music and an afternoon libatio
 n or two\, perhaps with an early supper or light bite . . . and don't forg
 et your dancing shoes!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nView this post on Instagra
 m\n\n\n\nA post shared by Uncle Paul (@unclepaul.music)\n\n\n\n\n\nhttps:/
 /youtu.be/kkkFP4I_sss?si=gzGWPrV77QLh1-Bg\n\n
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://jackofthewood.com/wp-content/uploads/202
 5/11/JOTW_SAT-NobodysDarling_2025_IG_1080x1350.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Jack of the Wood
UID:12220@jackofthewood.com
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260926T203000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260926T233000
DTSTAMP:20260824T210931Z
URL:https://jackofthewood.com/events/mr-jimmy-4/
SUMMARY:Mr. Jimmy
DESCRIPTION:\nMr Jimmy is guitarist / vocalist / songwriter\,&nbsp\; Jim 
 “Ang” Anderson\, who has fronted The Chicago Kingsnakes Blues band for
  35 years\, to&nbsp\;date performing over 4000 shows.\n\n\n\nMr Jimmy writ
 es\, sings and plays real-deal Blues\, Chicago style.&nbsp\; A lifelong re
 sident of the city's infamous South Side\, he has shared the stage with Bu
 ddy Guy\, Koko Taylor\, Little Milton\, James Cotton\, Junior Wells\, Left
 y Dizz\,&nbsp\; Jimmy Dawkins\, Johnny Twist\, and the list goes on... In 
 addition to his live performances\, he&nbsp\;has released&nbsp\;10 albums 
 of original music with the Chicago Kingsnakes and&nbsp\;was pleased to ann
 ounce his debut solo release “All Alone With the Blues” in July 2020. 
 \n\n\n\nDespite a rigorous recording and performance schedule\, Mr. Jimmy 
 still found time to produce and host an NPR radio show entitled “Confess
 in' The Blues” where he interviewed and performed with numerous Blues ar
 tists.\n\n\n\n&nbsp\;In 2024 Mr Jimmy was voted one of the Best Blues Perf
 ormers by the readers of Asheville's Mountain Xpress newspaper for the thi
 rd year in a row\n\n\n\nShow 8:30-11:30pm\, $10 cover at the door.\n\n\n\n
 \nhttps://youtu.be/edo8LXNPbnQ?si=1DIt9A9ZvpZcOIY8\n\n\n\n\n\nhttps://yout
 u.be/FUF2GGXJlqg?si=mGPDS6_E3TpNaxNX\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://jackofthewood.com/wp-content/uploads/202
 6/08/09-26-26_MrJimmy_IG_1080x1440-2.jpg
END:VEVENT
